Here's my take on the situation. I've been playing NH (vanilla only)
since 1993 (v3.1). I've been playing on NAO since Jan '07 and have won
21 times out of 178 games played so far, which includes at least one
ascension for every race, role, and gender, and a number of multiple-
conduct ascensions to boot. In all of those ascensions, I have not
burned a single amulet of life saving. However, I have *worn* an AoLS
in some of those, and I have usually carried spares whether I am
wearing one or not. When I'm not wearing an AoLS, I'm wearing an
amulet of reflection. I don't believe I've ever worn an amulet of ESP
to the high altar.

I like casting spells and I like doing it whether I play a spellcaster
role or not. I also do not wish for quest artifacts, and I don't rely
on my own quest artifact or MagicBane alone for magic resistance.
That's my playstyle and preference. Therefore I am most often wearing
GDSM + robe + AoR. Sometimes I am wearing SDSM + CoMR + AoLS, if I
don't need the spellcasting boost from the robe. In these cases, I
could wear ESP, but I prefer the extra insurance from the AoLS.

